Needs a live PostgreSQL warehouse: the `warehouse` datasource auto-connects on
startup, so without one the app logs a connect ERROR and the shared "clean
startup" check fails. The dataset is a 500k-employee simulation (gold marts over
a silver star schema), far too large to ship or seed on a CI runner.

It also needs a vantage-ui build carrying the 0.36 dashboard grammar
(`args`/`search:`/`group:`/`placeholder:` on selects, grids and charts). The
published-binary runner pins an older release, which fails schema validation on
every page here.

Run it explicitly against a local warehouse and a matching build:
  cargo run -p test-framework -- apps/cashgpt
